  "independent_source_audit": {
    "column7_has_no_rail": true,
    "carrier_separation_proof": "grid7 contains no kraubslpehi* tile in column 7. tmhxwcojkh moves a carrier one cell only when the destination contains kraubslpehi, so by induction no carrier can enter or cross column 7.",
    "why_carrier_separation_does_not_imply_peg_separation": "The static socket at (7,8) is a legal landing. With plain at (5,8) and red at (6,8), plain jumps to (7,8); red then jumps to (8,8); plain then jumps to (9,8). Because their names differ, cfilhtifcb removes neither crossed peg.",
    "win_rule": "cfilhtifcb decrements the projected plain-peg count only when the crossed peg name equals the jumper name; L7 wins when the projected count reaches 2. The final east plain jumps over the transported west plain, so exactly one same-name plain is removed.",
    "action_space_complete": "ACTION1-4 are carrier moves, ACTION6 selects/executes jumps, ACTION5 only arms the level reset keyhole, and ACTION7 is undo. Reset and undo add no new physical state needed by this route."
  },
  "round13_null_refutation": {
